es everywhere","touches":["hills","town"]},{"theme":"dinosaurs","n":1,"gist":"bring back dinosaurs","touches":["hills","walkers"]},{"theme":"life-better","n":1,"gist":"life gets better honestly","touches":["lamps","town"]},{"theme":"jobs-vanish","n":1,"gist":"jobs will disappear","touches":["walkers","square"]}],"set":[{"id":"town","params":[{"name":"lit","value":0.8}]}],"add":[],"remove":[],"draw":[{"id":"hills","theme":"data-centres","layer":1,"brief":"REWRITE opening landmark hills (keep its look). Grim: the horizon hills are now crowded with windowless grey data-centre slabs, huge, fenced, humming with blinking lights and exhaust plumes, climbing the hills from x 0 to 1600 behind the town. p.w makes them more numerous and taller. At least one slab grows through the hillside."},{"id":"dinosaur","theme":"dinosaurs","layer":4,"brief":"BRAND NEW. Playful: a huge friendly long-necked dinosaur wading in the sea behind the square, x 150-700, tall as the buildings, its neck leaning over the town, nibbling a lamp post or chimney and swinging its tail. Looks past the data centres on the hills; walkers wave. Box about 150,260,600,420. p.w grows it."},{"id":"lamps","theme":"life-better","layer":5,"brief":"REWRITE lamps (keep three posts). Idealised: warm, hopeful. Lamps now glow bigger and golden, strung with garlands of light across the square, with little glowing helper orbs floating between them and flowers climbing the posts. Also move them slightly to the back of the square (base y 740) so they overlap the walkers less. p.w widens the glow."},{"id":"walkers","theme":"jobs-vanish","layer":6,"brief":"REWRITE walkers (keep strolling townsfolk). Unease: the crowd thins as p.w rises; some walkers are faded ghost outlines, a few stand idle with bowed heads and empty hands beside a row of empty workbenches/stalls at the square edge, while a smooth glowing machine arm works on. Keep people always moving."}],"note":"The seaside town is filling with humming data centres and a ge